tools/__pycache__/
*.pyc
codex_out_*.md
sol_*.md

# private working notes (never publish)
PROGRESS.md
review_baseline/

# scratch text dumps left by PDF-extraction subagents (repo root only — real
# content such as spillovers/excluded_studies.txt lives in subfolders)
/*_intro.txt
/*_concl.txt
/*_head.txt
/*_tail.txt
/*_out.txt
/*_full.txt
/*_ctx*.txt

# Subagents reading PDFs keep writing scratch dumps into the repo root under
# ad-hoc names (foo_intro.txt, cl_p0.txt, ...). Ignore root-level .txt wholesale
# and re-admit the three that belong to the site. Tracked files are unaffected
# by .gitignore, so this cannot drop llms.txt / robots.txt from the deploy.
/*.txt
!/llms.txt
!/llms-full.txt
!/robots.txt
# the IndexNow key file (its name IS the key); tracked, but be explicit
!/6c841b23e12756bf2f1491dbd661cd2d.txt

# Build scratch: a byte-identical duplicate of /api/v1/ and /data/v1/.
data_layer/out/

# Scratch side-output of data_layer/93_codegrep.py. 13_publish.py already skips it
# by name, so the release is unaffected -- this only stops `git add -A` committing
# it into a public repo.
data_layer/codegrep_evidence.json

# The hand-built Zenodo bundle. 12_zenodo_bundle.py writes it to the repo ROOT, which in
# this layout is the live site, so an unguarded `git add -A` would publish a ~14 MB
# duplicate of the deposit into the public tree.
/zenodo_deposit/

# Mechanical drafts from tools/draft_transcript.py. The finished transcript is
# <project>.md and is committed; the .draft.md beside it is an intermediate a
# conversion agent regenerates whenever it wants one, and several agents work on
# the same paper at once, so committing them would just record whoever wrote last.
tools/transcripts/*.draft.md

# Dropbox writes a "conflicted copy" beside any file edited on two machines, and this
# tree lives in Dropbox. Each one is a stale duplicate sitting next to the real page, so
# an unguarded `git add -A` would publish an old copy of /about/ at a public URL. Two are
# in the tree right now. Tracked files are unaffected by .gitignore, so this cannot drop
# anything the site actually serves.
*conflicted copy*

# pdftotext dumps left beside a paper by a conversion agent. The /*.txt rule above only
# reaches the repo root; these land in the paper's own folder (discrate/discrate.pdf.txt).
*.pdf.txt
